#
# Counter-example for math:IncompleteCredibleIntervalShape (Rule I5): a
# math:CredibleInterval naming its posterior context through math:hasPosterior (so the
# posterior arm's sh:minCount 1 is SATISFIED) but omitting math:credibleMass, tripping the
# mass arm's sh:minCount 1 — shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (math:IncompleteCredibleInterval).
# Single violation: its posterior is a well-formed math:PosteriorDistribution (family
# named, no supplied parameters) so no distribution gate fires, and it is NOT typed
# math:ConfidenceInterval so no confidence-interval or conflation shape targets it —
# EXACTLY ONE finding, no sibling fires.
# Back-reference: math:IncompleteCredibleInterval (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Negative counterpart of conformance-fixtures/credible-interval-complete.ttl.
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecCredibleIntervalIncomplete).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:masslessCredible a math:CredibleInterval ;
    math:hasIntervalBound ex:credLower , ex:credUpper ;
    math:hasPosterior ex:paramPosterior .    # posterior present, but NO math:credibleMass

ex:credLower a math:MathematicalObject .
ex:credUpper a math:MathematicalObject .

# The posterior: a well-formed distribution, so no distribution gate fires.
ex:paramPosterior a math:PosteriorDistribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:betaFamily .

ex:betaFamily a math:DistributionFamily .
